5187	Ironwheel Village's Request
5188	Defeat 20 rusty murklings on the windmill isles
5189	So you're the Mender who brought back Dandelion Isle's wind! Rode the Windway all the way here, did you.
5190	This is Ironwheel Village, in the Rusty Windmill Isles. Since the windmills stopped, rust flufflings and scythe scarecrows are everywhere.
5191	Deal with twenty of them first. Then the villagers can go out to the fields.
5192	Ho ho, folks are back in the fields. You're as good as they say.
5193	The Chain Bridge
5194	Collect 4 Chain Links from Cog Nestkeepers and reconnect the chain bridge east of Middle Windmill Isle
5195	There was a chain bridge east of Middle Windmill Isle, but the chain snapped the day the great windmill turned backwards.
5196	Cog Nestkeepers nest on every windmill island, hoarding broken chain links. Four will reconnect the bridge.
5197	The chain bridge is whole again! Beyond it lies Chain Ferry, and then Great Windmill Isle…
5198	That's where the Creaking Warden is. Steel yourself.
5199	The Scarecrow Field
5200	Defeat 12 Scythe Scarecrows
5201	It's Solbaram, I followed the Windway too! Seen the scarecrows here? They used to be good kids that only chased birds.
5202	With the wind gone, they spin their scythe hands and attack people. When a round marker shows on the ground, back off fast. Let twelve of them rest.
5203	Thank you. The fields smell of wind again. Here's a ring I found.
5204	Scraping off Rust
5205	Bring 5 Rusty Cogs
5206	I'm Pulmu, the smith here. I've heard about that Musoe fellow.
5207	Rust flufflings and nail pods carry around cogs that fell out of the windmills. Bring me five and I'll teach you how to scrape off rust.
5208	Good, polish them well and they turn like new. For your trouble, a blessed whetstone and blessed glue.
5209	The Creaking Warden of Great Windmill Isle
5210	Defeat the Creaking Warden of Great Windmill Isle and touch its Pinwheel Beacon
5211	The warden of the great windmill has gone mad. It spins the blades on its back in reverse, sucking up all the isles' wind.
5212	It sweeps around with its blades and slams the ground in a line with chain fists. It summons nail pods too.
5213	When enraged, wind blades fly out in every direction. Dodge through the gaps between them.
5214	…The windmills are turning! One by one, the isles' windmills are spinning again!
5215	Thank you, Mender. But looking where the wind flows… the sky over Anchored Harbor is strangely still.
5216	Millkeeper Daedeulbo
5217	Blacksmith Pulmu
5218	Rust flufflings and scarecrows are swarming every windmill island. Twenty, please.
5219	Cog Nestkeepers on the windmill islands hold the chain links. Gather four and go to the broken chain bridge east of Middle Windmill Isle.